{"name":"Rocky Ridge","hex":"#918c86","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rocky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Abounding in, or full of, rocks; consisting of rocks.","Like a rock; rigid, solid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily rocked; unstable.","Encountering many problems; difficult, troubled; also, in danger or distress."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocky"},{"term":"ridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The back of any animal; especially the upper or projecting part of the back of a quadruped.","Any extended protuberance; a projecting line or strip."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form into a ridge.","To extend in ridges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocky Ridge, Calgary","blocks":[{"text":"Rocky Ridge is a residential neighbourhood in the northwest quadrant of Calgary, Alberta. It is located at the western edge of the city, and is bounded to the north by Country Hills Boulevard, to the east by Rocky Ridge Road, to the south by Crowchild Trail and to the west by Twelve Mile Coulee Road."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky_Ridge%2C_Calgary"},{"title":"Rocky Ridge (California)","blocks":[{"text":"Rocky Ridge is a 2,020 ft (620 m) ridge in the Inner Coast Ranges in western Contra Costa County, California, in the San Francisco Bay Area. Being the second-highest mountain in the county, it is visible from much of the surrounding area. The ridge is a very prominent feature in the geography of the towns of Lafayette, Moraga and Orinda, California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Rocky_Ridge_Sunset.png/330px-Rocky_Ridge_Sunset.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky_Ridge_(California)"},{"title":"Rocky","blocks":[{"text":"Rocky is a 1976 American sports drama film directed by John G. Avildsen and written 