ing the Spring wildflower bloom. (April 1, 2021)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARocky_Ridge_during_the_spring_bloom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png/500px-South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png/1280px-South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png/500px-South_from_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view south from atop Rocky Ridge towards Alameda County and the valleys of Kaiser, Cull and Crow creeks. The region about Rocky Ridge represents one of the last large areas of undeveloped land in the East Bay (May 25, 2023)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouth_from_Rocky_Ridge.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png/500px-Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png/1280px-Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png/500px-Mount_Diablo%2C_Las_Trampas_Peak_and_Rocky_Ridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view south and east from Round Top (1,764') in the Berkeley Hills, showing Rocky Ridge and its neighboring mountains. From left to right: Mount Diablo (3,449'), Las Trampas Peak (1,827') and Rocky Ridge (2,024') 